; Release builds for Linux link statically against musl, so the binary runs
; on a machine with no OCaml, no wand tree and no matching libc. Static
; linking is a Linux-only idea -- macOS does not support it and does not need
; it -- so it lives in a profile the macOS jobs do not use. Scoped to this
; directory: the stdlib table's generator runs on the build machine and has
; no reason to be linked this way.

; `-no-pie` is not incidental. Alpine's gcc defaults to PIE, so `-static`
; alone yields a static-pie binary, and the x86_64 one segfaults before it
; prints anything -- OCaml's runtime and musl's static-pie startup disagree.
; The aarch64 build of the same commit runs fine, which is how this stays
; hidden unless both are tested.

(env
 (static
  (link_flags
   (-ccopt -static -ccopt -no-pie))))

(executable
 (public_name wand)
 (name wand)
 (modules wand)
 (libraries wand))
